## Why This Is Asked
The question probes practical edge device security, supply chain controls, and IR readiness for OTA updates in a fleet setting.

## Key Concepts
- Hardware root of trust and device attestation
- Per-release key rotation and role separation
- SBOMs and artifact signing for OTA safety
- OTA gateway revocation and device rollback
- Incident response, containment, and forensics timelines

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation: verify OTA signature before flash
function verifyAndApply(image, publicKey) {
  const ok = verifySignature(image, publicKey);
  if (!ok) throw new Error('Invalid OTA signature');
  flash(image);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale key rotation across millions of devices?
- What logging and forensics data would you collect for IR?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests basic data protection practices for logging in a multi-tenant analytics platform, focusing on practical steps to prevent credential leakage without overhauling the system.

## Key Concepts

- Log redaction and sanitization
- Structured logging and ingestion pipelines
- Per-tenant data masking
- Token rotation policies
- Incident response basics for credential leakage

## Code Example

```javascript
function redactLog(event){
  try {
    const s = JSON.stringify(event);
    return s.replace(/token=[^\s&]+/gi, 'token=REDACTED');
  } catch (e) {
    return '{}';
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the log redaction in CI/CD?
- What adjustments if logs are stored in a non-text format (e.g., binary)?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical application of confidential computing to multi-tenant isolation in real-time ML workloads, beyond token-based controls.

## Key Concepts
- Confidential computing (TDX/Nitro/SEV)
- Per-tenant attested enclaves and key management
- Envelope encryption of in-flight data and outputs
- Attestation-based admission control at API gateway
- IR playbook with measurable success criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-spec showing attestation flow
function attestedInference(req, enclave) {
  if (!enclave.attest(req.tenant)) throw new Error('Untrusted tenant');
  const input = enclave.declassify(req.input, req.tenant);
  const out = enclave.infer(input);
  return enclave.envelope(out, req.tenant);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate per-tenant keys without service downtime?
- How would you detect and respond to a compromised enclave?
